This recipe runs an unmodified SGLang image, lmsysorg/sglang:dev-inkling-2-small, and adds Python hooks that are
mounted into the container and imported at interpreter start (patches/). The hooks, the launcher, the watchdog, the
benches and the documentation were written for this recipe; the third-party material below is adapted under its own
licence. Apart from the three short functions named under patches/stable_kernels.py, nothing third-party is
redistributed.

Adapted third-party code (modified for this recipe; the original notices apply to those parts):
  - patches/roce_collectives.py: a port to SGLang's GroupCoordinator of the vLLM adapter b12x_roce_all_reduce.py by
    Jason (@original-el8), github.com/local-inference-lab/vllm pull request 597. Copyright contributors to the vLLM
    project. Apache License 2.0. It drives the b12x RoCE runtime bundled in the image's FlashInfer (Apache-2.0).
  - patches/sitecustomize.py: the served-alias route handlers mirror SGLang's http_server.py originals (ported from
    this repository's DeepSeek-V4.1 recipe, overlay/served_aliases.py). Copyright SGLang Team. Apache License 2.0.
  - patches/paged_decode.py and patches/draft_decode.py: rebuild SGLang's Triton decode kernel from the source inside
    the image at import, with the page lookup (and, for the draft's reader, the masks) changed; they carry no copy of
    that source. patches/fa4_bias_far.py does the same for the SM120 FA4 forward kernel (the loop over the key
    blocks split, the far blocks compiled without the bias state). patches/fused_epilogue.py, fused_stream.py and
    fused_relbias.py are Triton kernels written for this recipe that reproduce, operation for operation, SGLang's
    short-convolution, residual-add, attn_res, RMSNorm and bias-shear kernels. The hooks in patches/sitecustomize.py,
    fi_moe.py, fi_mxfp8.py, prefill_glue.py, fp8_kv.py, dense_p12.py, dense_i8.py, tp_shard.py, spark_gate.py and
    sampled_lab.py wrap or replace functions of SGLang's Inkling model code and call its and FlashInfer's kernels.
    Copyright SGLang Team / FlashInfer contributors. Apache License 2.0.
  - patches/stable_kernels.py: modified copies of three short Triton functions of SGLang
    (sglang/kernels/ops/inkling2/attention.py: _tau_kernel, _gate_sink_kernel, _sigmoid), with the batch's row count
    and strides turned from compile-time constants into arguments; the file states the change. Copyright SGLang
    Team. Apache License 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
  - launch/relaunch-inkling2.sh and launch/watchdog-inkling2.sh: adapted from this repository's DeepSeek-V4.1 recipe
    (launch/relaunch.sh, launch/watchdog.sh; same author, MIT).

Method references (no code taken): block verification follows Sun et al., "Block Verification Accelerates
Speculative Decoding", arXiv 2403.10444 (bench/bv_exact.py checks it under this recipe's gate).

Not part of this repository: SGLang (Apache-2.0), FlashInfer (Apache-2.0), PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), Triton (MIT),
NVIDIA CUDA components (NVIDIA EULA). They come from the image, which is used unmodified under its own licences.
